<%# One catalogue card, shared by every index.

  The card links to the entry's own page when it has one. TikTok is the single entry that does not: the
  inventory's verdict is "mention only, labelled beta", so it keeps its card, its badge and its prerequisite
  and links nowhere -- which is honest, and still not a dead link.

  THE PREREQUISITE IS THE POINT OF THE CARD, not a footnote on it: "you need a WhatsApp Business account" is
  the sentence that decides whether a reader can use this channel today. It sits on its own tinted strip at
  the foot of the card, where the eye lands last and the answer is waiting.

  THE WHOLE CARD IS THE TARGET, AND ONLY WHEN THERE IS SOMEWHERE TO GO. Two defects met here. The border lit
  up on hover on every card, including the seven across /integrations and /channels that link nowhere, so the
  page promised a destination it did not have; and on the cards that do link, the only clickable thing was the
  title -- a ~24px target on the page a reader opens on a phone. The title's `after:absolute after:inset-0`
  now stretches the one anchor over the positioned card, so the hit area is the affordance, and `group` (which
  nothing used before) is what carries the hover back to the title.
%>
<% links = entry.detail? %>
<article class="<%= class_names('flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-lyn-line bg-lyn-paper',
                               'group relative transition-colors hover:border-lyn-royal/40' => links) %>">
  <div class="flex grow flex-col p-5">
    <%= content_tag heading_level, class: 'flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-base font-semibold text-lyn-ink' do %>
      <% if links %>
        <a class="transition-colors after:absolute after:inset-0 group-hover:text-lyn-royal focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-lyn-blue"
           href="<%= marketing_entry_path(scope, entry) %>">
          <%= t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.name") %>
        </a>
      <% else %>
        <%= t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.name") %>
      <% end %>
      <%= render 'marketing/shared/state_badge', state: entry.state %>
    <% end %>

    <p class="mt-2 grow text-sm leading-[1.8] text-lyn-ink-soft">
      <%= t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.summary") %>
    </p>
  </div>

  <% if t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.requires", default: nil).present? %>
    <p class="border-t border-lyn-line bg-lyn-mist px-5 py-3 text-xs leading-[1.75] text-lyn-ink-soft">
      <span class="font-semibold text-lyn-ink">
        <%= t(scope == :channels ? 'marketing.state.you_supply' : 'marketing.state.requires') %>
      </span>
      <%= t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.requires") %>
    </p>
  <% end %>
</article>
